  "007": {
    "catalogue": "**007. Ordinary two-point correlations and the corrected Elliott conjecture.** Proves the ordinary two-point Chowla conjecture, with a bound $`O(X/(\\log X)^c)`$ for Liouville correlation sums along fixed nonproportional affine forms, where <i>c</i> &gt; 0 is absolute. More generally, proves the binary corrected Elliott conjecture for complex multiplicative functions bounded by one when one factor is uniformly nonpretentious against each fixed Dirichlet character times $`n^{it}`$ for $`|t|\\le X`$. ([Lean](lean/docs/007.md))",
